\par\par \b \uc2 Austria wants Slovenia to join euro in 2007-sources  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Boris Groendahl  \par \uc2 601 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 20 Januar 2006\par 16:36\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 VIENNA, Jan 20 (Reuters) - Austria will lobby European Union finance ministers next week to allow Slovenia to adopt the euro \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 2007, making it the first EU newcomer to join the euro, Austrian Finance Ministry sources said on Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The Baltic countries of Estonia and Lithuania, which along with Slovenia were the first to link their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the euro ahead of monetary union after the EU's 2004 expansion, are not yet ready, the sources told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 Slovenia, a small country to the south of Austria, already meets the criteria for euro membership -- a stable \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , low inflation and low budget deficits. But procedural quirks could delay the process and Austria is trying to remove them.  \par \par \uc2 "This should not be delayed just because of bureaucratic obstacles," one of the sources said. "They have done what they had to do, they are ready now."  \par \par \uc2 Austrian Finance Minister Karl-Heinz Grasser wants to decide about Slovenia under his country's EU presidency in the first half of the year. He will bring up the issue at next week's meeting of euro zone finance ministers, the sources said.  \par \par \uc2 Austria favours bringing forward to May the convergence reports written by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the European Commission, in which they assess whether Slovenia meets the requirements for joining the 12-nation \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  club.  \par \par \uc2 "The ECB has said it is ready to bring forward the report," another source said. "It looks as if the way is free for Slovenia to enter the euro in January 2007," the source said.  \par \par \uc2 Technically, a decision on Slovenia can only be made after it has been in the European Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM-2) that links the Slovene tolar to the euro for two years -- proving it can remain stable against the euro over that time period.  \par \par \uc2 Since Slovenia joined ERM-2 in late June 2004, a May recommendation on its readiness would be too early for the assessment. But this limit has been bent before.  \par \par \uc2 The ECB in 1998 issued a convergence report on Italy and Finland roughly six months before their two-year periods ended and said their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had been broadly stable without the need for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and were expected to remain so.  \par \par \uc2 READY  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  and finance ministry have both said the former Yugoslav country is ready for euro entry next year.  \par \par \uc2 When Slovenia joined the exchange rate mechanism the central parity of the tolar was set at 239.64 to the euro. It has been stable since.  \par \par \uc2 The country meets euro entry requirements for public debt, budget deficit and interest rates and in November managed to bring its inflation down to the maximum level allowed for those who want to adopt the euro.  \par \par \uc2 However, neither Lithuania and Estonia currently meet the euro criteria, European Monetary Affairs Commissioner Joaquin Almunia said on Thursday, and Estonia has already said it would rather wait.  \par \par \uc2 "If the assessment were made today, with the (inflation) numbers published by Eurostat this morning, neither Estonia nor Lithuania would meet the criterion," Almunia said.  \par \par \uc2 Estonia, where inflation is at 3.7 percent, would prefer October or November for the evaluation, said finance ministry deputy under secretary Ranaldo Mandmets -- which practically rules out joining in 2007.  \par \par \uc2 But Lithuanian finance ministry adviser Ricardas Slapsys, looking at an inflation rate of 3 percent in December, said he still held hopes: "Lithuania will probably be able to adopt the euro according to our planned date."  \par \par \uc2 EU-ECONOMY-SLOVENIA|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|G|BNX  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060120e21k001gk\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 First Year of ERM II Smooth for Slovenia  \b0\par\par\uc2 sm/bdo/gj  \par \uc2 789 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 Juni 2005\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o  \par \par \uc2 Ljubljana, 18 June (STA) - It will be one year on 28 June since Slovenia  \par \par \uc2 joined the ERM II exchange rate mechanism, the waiting room for the euro.  \par \par \uc2 There have been no shake-ups so far: the exchange rate is steadily  \par \par \uc2 hovering around the central parity rate of SIT 239.64 per euro, and the  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has had to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  only once on the monetary market.  \par \par \uc2 "The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  assesses the first year in the ERM II as successful.  \par \par \uc2 Economic growth, the situation in individual markets and preserved  \par \par \uc2 macroeconomic balances confirm that the preceding adjustment to the  \par \par \uc2 business conditions maintained in Europe by the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was  \par \par \uc2 sustainable," \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  Vice-Governor Andrej Rant told STA.  \par \par \uc2 The exchange rate has remained close to the central parity rate throughout  \par \par \uc2 the year. The market rate was at SIT 239.54 on Friday and has been just  \par \par \uc2 below the parity rate since the end of April. According to \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 data, the average gap between the market and parity rates has been 0.01%.  \par \par \uc2 The bank \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the market just once, one month after ERM II entry,  \par \par \uc2 when it sold \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to respond to rate growth.  \par \par \uc2 According to Rant, "this \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  arose from a need for a signal that  \par \par \uc2 the existing concept of exchange rate policy had indeed been brought to an  \par \par \uc2 end with Slovenia's entry in the ERM II." He says the banks were initially  \par \par \uc2 complacent, so they were given the signal.  \par \par \uc2 Slovenia intends to introduce the euro on 1 January 2007 according to the  \par \par \uc2 "big bang" scenario of overnight changeover. Banks will accept tolar bills  \par \par \uc2 until February 2007, while the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will impose no limitations.  \par \par \uc2 The reason why Slovenia opted for this scenario is the good experience  \par \par \uc2 that it had when Yugoslav dinars were replaced first by coupons and then  \par \par \uc2 by tolars in the early 90s. Moreover, the ECB has assessed that two months  \par \par \uc2 of dual legal tender in the 12 members that introduced the euro in 2002 was  \par \par \uc2 too long.  \par \par \uc2 To be eligible for the euro, Slovenia has to stay in the ERM II for  \par \par \uc2 another year and keep the exchange rate within plus or minus 15% of the  \par \par \uc2 central parity rate. Moreover, it has to fulfil the convergence criteria  \par \par \uc2 of low inflation, public debt and interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Efforts to meet the criteria have been successful so far, except for  \par \par \uc2 inflation, which is only slowly coming down to the desired level. In May,  \par \par \uc2 inflation was 0.9 percentage points above the Maastricht threshold for  \par \par \uc2 that month.  \par \par \uc2 Yet the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is confident that inflation will be curbed  \par \par \uc2 sufficiently in time. "The forecasts of the Bank of Slovenia as well as  \par \par \uc2 other domestic and foreign institutions show that Slovenia will meet the  \par \par \uc2 inflation criterion in the reference period," Rant said.  \par \par \uc2 While inflation is the only criterion that Slovenia is yet to fulfil, the  \par \par \uc2 one-year reference period starting in June will be challenging  \par \par \uc2 nevertheless. The EU has noted that figures are not all that counts: the  \par \par \uc2 country's overall economic condition will also undergo thorough scrutiny.  \par \par \uc2 According to Rant, the second year in the ERM II will require close  \par \par \uc2 monitoring of wages and productivity. "The occurrence of a negative gap  \par \par \uc2 between the two is not a good sign," he emphasised. The focus will  \par \par \uc2 therefore be on current actions in ensuring the stability of public  \par \par \uc2 finances and managing labour costs.  \par \par \uc2 "Considering the uncertain oil prices, cost management is especially  \par \par \uc2 important and the changed economic conditions with forecasts of lower  \par \par \uc2 economic growth in Europe will be a challenge for public finances. Their  \par \par \uc2 flexibility could be put to a test," Rant added.  \par \par \uc2 Slovenia is gearing up for the euro in other areas as well. Companies do  \par \par \uc2 not expect any major shocks, as most are already doing business with  \par \par \uc2 eurozone countries. Moreover, over 60 percent of all exports end up in the  \par \par \uc2 EU.  \par \par \uc2 Indeed, businessmen expect benefits rather then difficulties, notably  \par \par \uc2 lower overhead costs, lower risk and greater attraction for foreign  \par \par \uc2 investment. Some problems are expected in the public and service sectors,  \par \par \uc2 especially retail.  \par \par \uc2 A heated debate has been under way about double pricing. Retailers  \par \par \uc2 initially insisted that double price tags are out of the question until  \par \par \uc2 the exchange rate is cemented, but this is theoretically possible only  \par \par \uc2 after the two-year ERM II period expires.  \par \par \uc2 The government and the Bank of Slovenia have come up with a solution that  \par \par \uc2 they believe will provide sufficient information for consumers while not  \par \par \uc2 putting too much pressure on retailers: price labels will include euros as  \par \par \uc2 of March 2006 according to the central parity rate, while double price tags  \par \par \uc2 will remain in place six months after the changeover to the euro.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument STA0000020050618e16i000p2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
