\par\par \b \uc2 Signs of Slovenian success in steadying tolar-Buba.   \b0\par\par\uc2 404 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2004\par 17:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2  FRANKFURT, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Slovenia is having some success in halting its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation, which is important to the country's future adoption of the euro, the Bundesbank said on Monday.    \par \par \uc2  Slovenia joined the Exchange Rate Mechanism ERM-2 in June, linking its tolar in a trading band against the euro to test whether it can keep the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  stable for at least two years before converting to the euro.    \par \par \uc2  The tolar has depreciated a little, prompting \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .    \par \par \uc2  "It will be decisive for \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's successful participation in ERM-2 whether the depreciating trend of the tolar against the euro can be credibly broken," the Bundesbank said in its August monthly report.    \par \par \uc2  "The first signs are thoroughly encouraging, even if the time period under consideration so far is very short," it added.    \par \par \uc2  Slovenia, along with Baltic EU members Estonia and Lithuania, joined ERM-2 on June 27. The three were among 10 countries, mainly in central Europe, that joined the EU in May this year.    \par \par \uc2  Slovenia set a central parity of 239.64 tolar to the euro when it joined ERM-2. ERM-2 members are required to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  if their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciate or depreciate by more than 15 percent from the central parity against the euro.    \par \par \uc2  The tolar had depreciated by 21 percent against the euro between the launch of the single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in 1999 and Slovenia's joining ERM-2 in June, the Bundesbank said.    \par \par \uc2  However, it noted that the tolar  had recently been trading at 240 to the euro, just 0.15 percent weaker than its central parity.    \par \par \uc2  "The euro-tolar exchange rate therefore has been moving in a very narrow band so far, without having to make use of the permitted plus/minus 15 percent fluctuation margin around the central rate," the Bundesbank said.    \par \par \uc2  The Bundesbank said that further tension-free development of the exchange rates of the tolar as well as the Estonian and Lithuanian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  depended on those countries maintaining stability-oriented economic policies, particularly for government budgets, and carrying out structural reforms.    \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  late last month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time to support the tolar.    \par \par \uc2  One \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trader said he saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  more as a training manoeuvre and said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was trying to defend an unofficial and self-imposed 0.2 percent band for the tolar.    \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040816e08g00fw9\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2 News Roundup - Tuesday, 27 July  \b0\par\par\uc2 vh/gj/td/mo/mlj/np/kko/arh/uk/vh  \par \uc2 1,785 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2004\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o  \par \par \uc2 Ljubljana, 27 July (STA) - Below is a roundup of major events on Tuesday,  \par \par \uc2 27 July:  \par \par \uc2 POLITICS  \par \par \uc2 BERLIN, Germany - International topics were at the forefront of Tuesday's  \par \par \uc2 talks between Foreign Minister Ivo Vajgl and his German counterpart  \par \par \uc2 Joschka Fischer. As Vajgl told STA, the pair focused on bilateral  \par \par \uc2 cooperation in the EU, issues related to the EU's common security and  \par \par \uc2 foreign policy, the future of OSCE, the Middle East and the Western  \par \par \uc2 Balkans. Relations between Slovenia and Germany are problem-free, while  \par \par \uc2 cooperation in economy, politics and culture has been developing well,  \par \par \uc2 Vajgl said he and his counterpart established. According to him, Germany  \par \par \uc2 supports Slovenia's admission to the Organisation for Economic Cooperation  \par \par \uc2 and Development. The minister also said he proposed signing a bilateral  \par \par \uc2 accord on free movement of labour.  \par \par \uc2 BERN, Switzerland - Slovenia and Switzerland signed agreements on fighting  \par \par \uc2 organised crime, the return of illegal residents, and deployment of  \par \par \uc2 liaison officers, as Interior Minister Rado Bohinc met his Swiss  \par \par \uc2 counterpart Cristoph Blocher in Bern on Tuesday. As Minister Bohinc told  \par \par \uc2 STA, the agreements will further upgrade cooperation between the Slovenian  \par \par \uc2 and Swiss police, making it more organised and efficient, as they will  \par \par \uc2 enable a faster and direct exchange of information. According to Bohinc,  \par \par \uc2 Slovenia as well as the countries to its north and west are exposed to  \par \par \uc2 criminal activities of the so-called Balkan route, including human, drugs  \par \par \uc2 and arms trafficking.  \par \par \uc2 PODGORICA, Serbia-Montenegro - Minister of Labour, Family and Social  \par \par \uc2 Affairs Vlado Dimovski is visiting Montenegro Tuesday and Wednesday at the  \par \par \uc2 invitation of his counterpart Slavoljub Stijepovic. The Labour Ministry  \par \par \uc2 says the purpose of the visit is to exchange experience and boost  \par \par \uc2 bilateral cooperation. Dimovski is expected to outline Slovenia's activity  \par \par \uc2 in the areas he is responsible for, in particular the country's experience  \par \par \uc2 in attaining EU standards in labour, family and social affairs, as well as  \par \par \uc2 employment and labour market policies. The two sides are further expected  \par \par \uc2 to share experiences with reforms, social security, pension and disability  \par \par \uc2 insurance. The visit is moreover seen as Slovenia's contribution to help  \par \par \uc2 Montenegro to promptly join the EU, the Labour Ministry stated in a press  \par \par \uc2 release.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - Responding to an invitation by Foreign Minister Ivo Vajgl,  \par \par \uc2 head of the government of the Italian border region Friuli-Venezia Giulia  \par \par \uc2 Riccardo Illy is due to arrive in Slovenia on Wednesday for talks  \par \par \uc2 dominated by problems faced by both ethnic minorities, transport issues  \par \par \uc2 and cross border cooperation. According to the Foreign Ministry, the  \par \par \uc2 purpose of the visit is to confirm the close relations between both sides  \par \par \uc2 and set the guidelines for future cooperation. Relations took on a new  \par \par \uc2 dimension with Slovenia's accession to the EU, offering new opportunities  \par \par \uc2 of taking cooperation to a higher level, the Foreign Ministry said in a  \par \par \uc2 press release prior to the visit.  \par \par \uc2 NOVO MESTO - Milos Kovacic, the outgoing CEO of the pharmaceutical company  \par \par \uc2 Krka, will stand at the parliamentary elections as the candidate of the  \par \par \uc2 ruling Liberal Democrats (LDS). As he told the press on Tuesday, "business  \par \par \uc2 diplomacy" will be very important for Slovenia in the coming years if the  \par \par \uc2 country wants to be successful in the EU, adding he had rich experience as  \par \par \uc2 he has been at the helm of Krka for 20 years. Gregor Golobic, the chair of  \par \par \uc2 the LDS council, refused to say whether there will be more company heads  \par \par \uc2 on the LDS list at the autumn elections. He said that talks with potential  \par \par \uc2 candidates were still underway and that the list would be completed by the  \par \par \uc2 end of August.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - Parliament Speaker Feri Horvat on Tuesday received Austrian  \par \par \uc2 Ambassador to Slovenia Ferdinand Mayrhofer-Gruenbuehl, thanking him for  \par \par \uc2 Austria's support in Slovenia's EU integration and for the swift aid  \par \par \uc2 offered in the wake of the Posocje earthquake earlier in July, the  \par \par \uc2 parliament said. The cooperation between Austria and Slovenia is well  \par \par \uc2 underway in all fields, particularly in economy. Horvat pointed out that  \par \par \uc2 bilateral trade amounts to almost EUR 2bn and that Austria is the biggest  \par \par \uc2 foreign investor in Slovenia, the parliament wrote in a press release.  \par \par \uc2 BUSINESS & ECONOMY  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - The mayor of the biggest financial centre in Europe said that  \par \par \uc2 Slovenia could act as a springboard for financial institutions wishing to  \par \par \uc2 do business in SE Europe. According to Robert Finch, the Lord Mayor of the  \par \par \uc2 City of London, there are many opportunities for cooperation between  \par \par \uc2 Slovenia and London City. Speaking at Tuesday's press conference after  \par \par \uc2 meeting PM Anton Rop, Finance Minister Dusan Mramor and Bank of Slovenia  \par \par \uc2 Governor Mitja Gaspari, Finch said the two sides should work for  \par \par \uc2 harmonisation in trade and greater cooperation between financial  \par \par \uc2 institutions. He said he would like to see London City involved in any  \par \par \uc2 possible second wave of privatisation in Slovenia, adding it was important  \par \par \uc2 to establish how London City could participate in the development of the  \par \par \uc2 Slovenian economy.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for  \par \par \uc2 the first time since \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the ERM II exchange rate mechanism,  \par \par \uc2 a grooming phase for the adoption of the euro. The bank sold euros - 20  \par \par \uc2 million according to some reports - in line with ERM II regulations, STA  \par \par \uc2 learnt from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials would not elaborate,  \par \par \uc2 but said the move was nothing out of the ordinary.Slovenia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 responded to the growth of the euro noted over the past week, the public  \par \par \uc2 radio broadcaster, Radio Slovenija, said. Analysts believe the sum in  \par \par \uc2 question is not substantial.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - A day after appointing Marko Simoneti as the head of the  \par \par \uc2 Ljubljana Stock Exchange (LJSE), the supervisory board of the LJSE came  \par \par \uc2 out to say that Simoneti was the best choice. According to Zdenko  \par \par \uc2 Podlesnik, the head of the LJSE supervisory board, Simoneti was chosen  \par \par \uc2 unanimously to replace outgoing LJSE director Drasko Veselinovic. Simoneti  \par \par \uc2 already resigned as a supervisory board member in order to assume the new  \par \par \uc2 post on 1 January 2005. According to Podlesnik, the major challenge in the  \par \par \uc2 future will be the development of the Ljubljana Stock Exchange. "Among  \par \par \uc2 other things, services comparable with that on foreign stock markets will  \par \par \uc2 have to be phased in."  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - A day after the management of the Slovenian Railways boasted  \par \par \uc2 upbeat half-year business figures with profits of EUR 2.55m, the utility's  \par \par \uc2 trade union said Tuesday that workers had been forced to work extra hours  \par \par \uc2 not envisaged in the collective agreement. The trade union highlighted in  \par \par \uc2 today's press release that workers were forced to work 40 or 50 extra  \par \par \uc2 hours per month due to lack of labour force. Moreover, not all workers are  \par \par \uc2 able to take a break during a working day, while their working hours are  \par \par \uc2 not in line with the collective agreement, according to the union.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - The Italian laboratory that examined bees found poisoned  \par \par \uc2 earlier in July has not found any traces of the substance contained in the  \par \par \uc2 disputed Gaucho pesticide but discovered the presence of two other  \par \par \uc2 substances, STA was told by the Agriculture Ministry, which will reveal  \par \par \uc2 the findings to the press on Friday. One substance was found from bees  \par \par \uc2 killed in the coastal region and a different one was detected in bees  \par \par \uc2 killed in the NW region of Gorenjsko, said Marina Rojko, the spokesperson  \par \par \uc2 at the Agriculture Ministry. The Veterinary Administration (VURS) is  \par \par \uc2 currently drafting conclusions, said Rojko, adding that veterinarians are  \par \par \uc2 to meet with beekeepers over the matter.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - There were a total of 12,291 job vacancies in Slovenian at the  \par \par \uc2 end of 2003, up 5.7 percent compared with a year earlier. This is stated  \par \par \uc2 in the first vacancies statistics report, released by the national  \par \par \uc2 Statistics Office to align its methodology with that of Eurostat. The  \par \par \uc2 report says most vacancies were available in manufacturing (3,109), retail  \par \par \uc2 (1,898) and construction (1,851). Quite a few vacancies were also in  \par \par \uc2 financial services (212) and public administration (271), while only four  \par \par \uc2 jobs were available in fisheries and only 11 in private households  \par \par \uc2 employing staff.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - The benchmark SBI 20 index gained 32.07 points or 0.7 percent  \par \par \uc2 on Tuesday to close the day at 4,610.47 points.  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - Optimism continued to prevail on the Ljubljana Stock Exchange,  \par \par \uc2 with the benchmark SBI 20 index gaining 32.07 points (0.7 percent) to  \par \par \uc2 close Tuesday's trading at 4,610.47 points. Despite the summer calm,  \par \par \uc2 volumes were moderate, amounting to SIT 1.04bn (EUR 4.34m), of which 40  \par \par \uc2 percent was done in four package deals.  \par \par \uc2 ARTS & CULTURE  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA - A music concert by the Slovenian band Bast opened the  \par \par \uc2 traditional summer Trnfest Festival on Tuesday evening at KUD France  \par \par \uc2 Preseren, an independent cultural centre in Ljubljana. Over a hundred  \par \par \uc2 events are scheduled to take place until 31 August, all free of charge.  \par \par \uc2 One of the most popular open-air events in Ljubljana, which last year  \par \par \uc2 attracted some 40,000 visitors, will offer music concerts, theatre  \par \par \uc2 performances and literary readings, exhibitions, films, a special  \par \par \uc2 programme for children and the international Emona Promenade.  \par \par \uc2 VIENNA, Austria - A novel by Slovenian writer Lojze Kovacic, who passed  \par \par \uc2 away earlier this year, tops the list of ten best novels composed by the  \par \par \uc2 Austrian public broadcaster ORF for August. "Die Zugereisten", the German  \par \par \uc2 translation of the novel "Prisleki" (The Newcomers), has been published by  \par \par \uc2 the Klagenfurt-based Drava publisher. In this autobiographical novel,  \par \par \uc2 Kovacic depicts his childhood - a life of poverty and misery. Fantasy and  \par \par \uc2 imagination are strongly at work in the perception of the young Lojzek,  \par \par \uc2 who in 1938 suddenly finds himself in Slovenia, the homeland of his  \par \par \uc2 father. The novel has already won acclaim at home; critics have namely  \par \par \uc2 selected it the novel of the 20th century.  \par \par \uc2 CRIME  \par \par \uc2 IVANCNA GORICA - A major source of water for a small Slovenian region is  \par \par \uc2 under threat after hundreds of litres of dangerous chemicals were dumped  \par \par \uc2 in its vicinity on Sunday. Police apprehended a 24-year-old man on Sunday  \par \par \uc2 after he was found dumping several drums containing an unknown substance  \par \par \uc2 in the vicinity of the Globocec spring on Sunday. The suspect supposedly  \par \par \uc2 slashed the barrels open and more than 1,000 litres of various substances  \par \par \uc2 are said to have leaked out. Tests carried out so far have shown no signs  \par \par \uc2 that the spring has been contaminated, although environmental experts say  \par \par \uc2 that it could take days for contamination to show.  \par \par \uc2 OBREZJE - In the latest drug bust on Slovenia's border with Croatia,  \par \par \uc2 customs officials seized 28.6 kilograms of heroin that was supposedly  \par \par \uc2 headed to Germany. Customs officers discovered the drug stash in a van  \par \par \uc2 driven by two Bosnian citizens who tried to cross into Slovenia at the  \par \par \uc2 Obrezje border crossing last Thursday, customs officials told the press on  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday.  \par \par \uc2 Dokument STA0000020040727e07r000dx\par }\page {\par\fs20\b  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank Intervenes \highlight\uc2  on  \highlight22\uc2 Currency \highlight\uc2  Market   \b0\par\par\uc2 gj/vh   \par \uc2 175 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2004\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o   \par \par \uc2 Ljubljana, 27 July (STA) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market for the first time since \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  entered the ERM II   \par \par \uc2 exchange rate mechanism, a grooming phase for the adoption of the euro.   \par \par \uc2 The bank sold euros - 20 million according to some reports - in line with   \par \par \uc2 ERM II regulations, STA learnt from the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \b \highlight22\uc2 Central bank\b0 \highlight\par \par \uc2 officials would not elaborate, but said the move was nothing out of the   \par \par \uc2 ordinary.   \par \par \uc2 Slovenia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  responded to the growth of the euro noted over the   \par \par \uc2 past week, the public radio broadcaster, Radio Slovenija, said. Analysts   \par \par \uc2 believe the sum in question is not substantial.   \par \par \uc2 Slovenia entered the ERM II on 28 June, setting a central euro-tolar rate   \par \par \uc2 at SIT 239.64. ERM II rules set that the exchange rate can fluctuate 15   \par \par \uc2 percent on either side of this rate.   \par \par \uc2 Today the tolar-euro rate stood at SIT 239.75, meaning that it has not   \par \par \uc2 shifted significantly from the set rate, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  added.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument STA0000020040727e07r000b5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
