\par\par \b \uc2 UPDATE 1-Slovenian cbank  \highlight22\uc2 intervenes \highlight\uc2  for first time since ERM-II.  \b0\par\par\uc2 310 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Juli 2004\par 16:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2004 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 LJUBLJANA, July 27 (Reuters) - \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2 's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support the tolar in the domestic \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday for the first time since joining the Exchange Rate Mechanism (ERM-2) last month as a step towards adopting the euro.  \par \par \uc2 "There was an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been selling \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," Gordana Pipan, spokeswoman for the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2 , told Reuters.  \par \par \uc2 "This was the first \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the open \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market (since ERM-2 entry), in line with the concept explained at Slovenia's entry into ERM-2," she added  \par \par \uc2 The Bank of Slovenia said it had sold foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  but declined to elaborate. Traders said the bank had sold 20 million euros.  \par \par \uc2 "There was some more buying than selling (of euros) last week and the exchange rate rose. So it is a bit surprising that this came today, I would have expected it yesterday or last week," one trader at Bank Austria-Creditanstalt said.  \par \par \uc2 "I see this (\b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 ) more as a training manoeuvre, since the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is trying to defend the unofficial and self-imposed 0.2 percent band for the tolar," he added.  \par \par \uc2 The tolar was trading at 239.89/240.01 at 1301 GMT. The central parity of Slovenia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  under ERM-II was set at 239.640 tolars per euro.  \par \par \uc2 The European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  set its upper and lower \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rates for the tolar at 275.586 tolar per euro and 203.694 tolar, respectively.  \par \par \uc2 European Union newcomers Slovenia, Estonia and Lithuania joined the ERM-2 at the end of June and became the first of 10 new EU members to join ERM-2, the block's waiting room for the euro which they plan to adopt at the start of 2007.   \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020040727e07r001y4\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
