\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia \highlight\uc2  ends  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 73 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par 14:56\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LJUBLJANA, Sept 18 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Monday it was ending its two-month \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market that was designed to slow down the tolar's depreciation. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  started on July 18 when the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  told commercial banks to buy euros at a minimum rate of 207.12 tolars and to sell at a maximum of 207.96 tolars. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010821dw9i07cpi\par }\page {\par\fs20\b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia \highlight\uc2 's  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  to Cease  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\uc2  in  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange \highlight\uc2  Market. \b0\par\par\uc2 197 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 18 September 2000\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o\par \par \uc2  Ljubljana, 18 September (STA) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will soon complete a two-month period of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market by setting a base exchange rate and a maximum ratio between the purchase and the selling rates. 21 banks which signed a co-\b \highlight22\uc2 operation\b0 \highlight\uc2  contract with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in March will therefore be able to set their purchase and selling exchange rates independently as of 19 September, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported on Monday. \par \par \uc2  The aim of such an \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was to curtail rapid increases of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  as the growth of exchange rates was estimated to be too fast at the time of the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  As of 18 July, the 21 contracting banks were obliged to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the corporate sector for a minimum of SIT 207.1249 per euro and sell \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for a maximum of SIT 207.9551 per euro. The highest ratio between the purchase and the selling rates was set at 0.2 percent. (konec)ar/eho STA023 2000-09-18/16:13. \par \par \uc2  (c) 2000 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o. \par \par \uc2 Dokument sta0000020010817dw9i0050s\par }\page {\par\fs20\b  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Will  \highlight22\uc2 Intervene \highlight\uc2  on the  \highlight22\uc2 Foreign Exchange \highlight\uc2  Market. \b0\par\par\uc2 267 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 Juli 2000\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2000 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o\par \par \uc2  Ljubljana, 17 July (STA) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market on Tuesday because it believes that the current growth in exchange rates is too high. According to a press release published on Monday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  fixed the base exchange rate at SIT 207.54 for one euro with a difference of up to 0.2 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is possible under a special contract signed between the Bank of Slovenia and 21 Slovene banks last March. \par \par \uc2  On the basis of the base exchange rate and the difference the lowest buying rate and the highest selling rate are calculated. The banks that signed the contract with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  are obliged to buy and sell at the agreed price. On the market serving companies \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be purchased at no less than SIT 207,1249 a euro and sold at up to SIT 207.9551 a euro as of 18 July. In exchange offices rates calculated in euro may differ up to 0.2 percent up from the highest selling rate and down from the lowest buying rate for the German mark and up to 0.4 percent for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  of the EMU members, Switzerland, Great Britain and the U.S. \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Slovenia will change the base exchange rate in line with trends on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market and domestic money market and in accordance to the goals of its monetary policy. (konec)ep STA013 2000-07-17/15:52. \par \par \uc2  (c) 2000 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o. \par \par \uc2 Dokument sta0000020010817dw7h003eg\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
