\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia central bank \highlight\uc2  ends  \highlight22\uc2 forex intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 168 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 23 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 1999\par 18:59\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1999 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LJUBLJANA, March 23 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Tuesday that it would end \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market as of Wednesday. \par \par \uc2  The bank started to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  on January 25 when it set commercial bank buying rate for the euro at 189.52 tolars, which was later raised three times. \par \par \uc2  On March 15, the rate was last raised to 190.6 tolars for the euro from 190.3 tolars. \par \par \uc2  During the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was buying \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from chosen commercial banks at an undisclosed rate. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  did not say why it decided to end the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  Analysts said the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which was designed to lower the value of the tolar against the euro, reached its target as the average commercial banks' rate for buying euros from companies rose to 190.55 tolars from 188.7 before the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  ((Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-17-00-545, ljubljana.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1999. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010909dv3n00t6k\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
