\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia \highlight\uc2  ends tolar rate  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2 . \b0\par\par\uc2 245 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1998\par 17:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LJUBLJANA, July 8 (Reuters) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  said on Wednesday it would on Thursday end the tolar exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  it began at the end of May. \par \par \uc2  "From July 9 the cooperating banks are no longer obliged to maintain the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  tolar exchange rate," the bank said in a statement. \par \par \uc2  At the end of May, the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said banks cooperating with its exchange rate \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  would have to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from companies at a minimum rate of 93.9 tolars to the German mark. \par \par \uc2  The minimum rate was raised to 94.1 on June 15 and to 94.4 on July 2. \par \par \uc2  Following the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the banks' exchange rate for companies rose to an average of about 94.5 tolars to the mark from 93.5 tolars at the end of May and 94.4 tolars at the start of the year. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would continue to buy \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from those commercial banks that bought at least 90 percent of all \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  from companies at a rate no lower than the last tolar \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  exchange rate. \par \par \uc2  Banks wanting to sell \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  to the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will also have to have a mark exchange rate for citizens no lower than 0.2 percent below the last \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  rate of 94.4 tolars. \par \par \uc2  ((Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-17-00-545, ljubljana.newsroom@reuters.com)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du7801epe\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2  Slovene  \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank \highlight\uc2  Has Stopped  \highlight22\uc2 Intervening \highlight\uc2  on Foreign Money Markets. \b0\par\par\uc2 178 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 8 Juli 1998\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o\par \par \uc2  Ljubljana, 8 July (STA) - The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  has said the period of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by setting purchase prices of foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  ended on Wednesday. The decision was adopted on Wednesday by the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor, following the bid for \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign money markets by means of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchase price dating from 27 May. The banks selected according to the bid are no longer obliged to keep up the \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchase price as of 9 July, the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  reported. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  on 2 July sent the bid for temporary \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  purchase of \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the obligatory return purchase in two months to those banks which have signed an agreement on cooperation in foreign money markets \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  with the Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2 . The banks were entitled to lower exchange rates for the purchase of foreign cash in exchange offices for a maximum of 0.2 percent for D-Mark, and 0.4 percent for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) 1998 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o. \par \par \uc2 Dokument sta0000020010927du780015f\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
