\par\par \b \uc2  Bank of  \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia intervenes \highlight\uc2  to slow tolar rise. \b0\par\par\uc2 295 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 29 Mai 1998\par 15:17\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 Reuters Limited\par \par \uc2  LJUBLJANA, May 29 (Reuters) - The Bank of Slovenia said on Friday from this week it would buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from five commercial banks at a minimum rate of 94.1 tolars to the mark to slow the appreciation of the tolar. \par \par \uc2  The rate for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  will be fixed according to their Frankfurt rate against mark, the bank said. \par \par \uc2  "We want to reduce the difference between tolar exchange rates and inflation. Since September the tolar has appreciated six to eight percent against the main \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in which we conduct our foreign trade," Francek Drenovec, head of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's analytic and research centre, told Reuters. \par \par \uc2  While the tolar had eased slightly on the foreign exchanges since September, in real terms it had appreciated substantially because of high domestic inflation, Drenovec said. \par \par \uc2  Slovenia's main foreign trade \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  are the German mark, Italian lira, Austrian shilling, French franc, Swiss franc, U.S. dollar and British pound. \par \par \uc2  On Friday the tolar stood at 93.47 to the mark, compared to 94.4 tolars at the start of 1998 and 92.63 tolars at the start of September 1997. \par \par \uc2  Slovenia's consumer price index rose by 8.8 percent in 1997, but in the first five months of 1998 it has risen a further 4.9 percent. \par \par \uc2  The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it would buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Nova Ljubljanska Banka, SKB  , Dolenjska Banka, Banka Celje and Abanka, who are in turn obliged to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  from companies at a minimum price of 93.9 tolars to the mark. \par \par \uc2  The five banks account for over 40 percent of Slovenia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  trade between banks and companies. ((Marja Novak, Ljubljana newsroom, 386-61-17-00-545)). \par \par \uc2  (C) Reuters Limited 1998. \par \par \uc2 Dokument lba0000020010925du5t0488y\par }\page {\par\fs20\b \uc2  Bank of Slovenia to Participate in Foreign Money Markets. \b0\par\par\uc2 277 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 27 Mai 1998\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 STA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 1998 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o\par \par \uc2  Ljubljana, 27 May (STA) - Bank of Slovenia's Council passed the following decisions at its 161st session on Monday: \par \par \uc2  The Bank of Slovenia will actively engage in foreign money markets. The banks that the Bank of Slovenia will sign cooperation agreements with after selecting them in public tenders will be allowed to purchase foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  at SIT 93.90 per Deutsche mark from 25 May onwards. \par \par \uc2  The selected banks will be entitled to lower exchange rates for the purchase of foreign cash in exchange offices for a maximum of 0.2 percent for Deutsche marks, and 0.4 percent for other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  The Bank of \b \highlight22\uc2 Slovenia\b0 \highlight\uc2  will have the right to change \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  conditions in accordance with foreign money market trends and monetary policy objectives. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  will inform the public about the selected banks, through which \b \highlight22\uc2 interventions\b0 \highlight\uc2  in foreign money markets will be conducted, on Thursday, 28 May. \par \par \uc2  The Council also amended the decision on the Bank of Slovenia unbalanced foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  assets and liabilities (the bank's open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  position), stipulating that the banks will have to balance their open foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  positions on a monthly basis. The decision will take effect upon publication in the Official Gazette. \par \par \uc2  The Council confirmed the June \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  minimum of SIT 362,934 million, down 0.3 percent from the previous month. \par \par \uc2  The Council also adopted the report on the use of contemporary payment instruments in the first quarter of 1998, pointing out bank risks the are increasingly present in the constantly rising volume of credit card \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 . \par \par \uc2  (c) 1998 STA, Slovenska Tiskovna Agencija d.o.o. \par \par \uc2 Dokument sta0000020010927du5r0012r\par }\par \b \uc2 Zusammenfassung der Suche\b0\par \par  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \uc2 Text\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\intbl\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 \li50\uc2 (foreign exchange or fx or forex or currenc*) and (interven* or operation*) and (Slovenia near10 interven*) and (rst=trtw or rst=tprw or rst=tdjw) and (central bank or ministry of finance or treasury ministry or monetary authority)\cell \pard \ql \li0\ri0\widctlpar\aspalpha\aspnum\faauto\adjustright\rin0\lin0 {  \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx2000\clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\brdrs \cellx9072\row } \trowd\trgaph15\trqc\trleft-15 \clvertalt\clbrdrt\brdrs\clbrdrl\brdrs\clbrdrb\brdrs\clbrdrr\